    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30844" root="عنى" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَانٍ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَنٍ</span>. [See also art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عنو</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  In the
phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَنَآءٌ عَانٍ</span>, it denotes intensiveness; [the
meaning being <i>Severe difficulty,</i> &amp;c.;] (K, TA;)
like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَاعِرٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَائِتٌ</span> in the phrases <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِعْرٌ شَاعِرٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَوْتٌ مَائِتٌ</span>: (TA:) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَنٍّ</span></b> ; (K, TA;)
in the M like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُكْرَمٌ</span> [i. e. ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْنًى</span></b> ]. (TA.)

